{
  "_readme": "PUBLIC product families (owner ruling 2026-10-21): the catalogue shows six CONFIGURABLE products, each ONE card with a configurator sheet, and every other published product stays a FIXED item (quantity + size + note only). This file is the single source of truth and holds NO price of any kind: each family lists its options, defaults and size limits, the published SKUs it ABSORBS (they no longer appear as their own cards; each maps to the closest configuration, which is also what a saved draft line is converted to), and its primary SKU (whose list price, with its own size rules, is the base the server prices from; the option amounts are kept in private staff data). \"fixed\" lists every published SKU that is NOT absorbed (the specialised items of Preparation, Washing and Storage are not published at all: scripts/public-categories.json excludedProducts, owner ruling 2026-10-21 (b)); scripts/build-catalogue.js refuses a published product that is in neither place, or in both. scripts/build-catalogue.js GENERATES js/qr-families.js (+ the byte-identical functions/qr-families.js), the catalogue cards, the data island and functions/qr-published.json from this file. Edit here, then run: node scripts/build-catalogue.js. Option values (v) are what is stored and validated; labels (l), summaries (s) and hints are what is shown. widthRule is the usual minimum length for the chosen options (hard: refused below it; otherwise guidance only). Preview rules (preview) build the file names of the owner's photo shot list, see docs/configurator-preview-photo-list.md.",
